+# Incidents brief
+
+Action status as of 30 September.
+
+## 11 August: ingest stall, full database disk
+
+- **Impact:** incoming data stopped for about 2.5 hours overnight; customers saw stale dashboards, no data lost.
+- **Cause:** one malformed batch jammed ingest, which retried it endlessly; the retry logs filled the database disk and writes were refused.
+- **Fix:** restarted ingest with the bad batch set aside, then cleaned up the database and old logs.
+- **Follow-ups:**
+  - Disk alert at 80% (Sunil): done.
+  - Stop bad batches jamming ingest (Jonas): open, in review.
+  - Paging escalation review (Mara, chair): done; pages now escalate after 15 minutes.
+
+## 21 September: expired API certificate
+
+- **Impact:** public API unreachable for 47 minutes; nearly all clients failed.
+- **Cause:** the certificate expired; its automatic renewal had failed silently for weeks because it held an outdated credential.
+- **Fix:** renewed the certificate and restarted the API; the renewal is fixed and now alerts on failure.
+- **Follow-ups:**
+  - Reminder 14 days before each expiry (Priya): done.
+  - Alert on days left (Priya): open.
+  - Expiry check in weekly checklist (Tomasz): open.
+  - Responders record steps as they go (Mara): done, in the handover notes.
